   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 352 of the laws of 2005, amending the education law\nrelating to implementation of the federal individuals with disabilities\neducation improvement act of 2004; to amend chapter 430 of the laws of 2006,\namending the education law relating to implementation of the federal\nindividuals with disabilities education improvement act of 2004; and to amend\nchapter 378 of the laws of 2007, amending the education law relating to the\nimplementation of the federal individuals with disabilities education\nimprovement act of 2004, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8331",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8331-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §22, Chap 352 of 2005; amd §8, Chap 430 of 2006; amd §27, Chap 378 of 2007",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8331\n\nSPONSOR: MARCELLINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 352 of the laws of 2005, amending the education\nlaw relating to implementation of the federal individuals with disabili-\nties education improvement act of 2004; to amend chapter 430 of the laws\nof 2006, amending the education law relating to implementation of the\nfederal individuals with disabilities education improvement act of 2004;\nand to amend chapter 378 of the laws of 2007, amending the education law\nrelating to the implementation of the federal individuals with disabili-\nties education improvement act of 2004, in relation to the effectiveness\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend, for three years, provisions that\nconform State Education Law to the federal Individuals with Disabilities\nEducation Act (IDEA) of 2004 in order to ensure that New York State will\ncontinue to be in compliance with federal IDEA requirements through the\n2020-2021 school year.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSections 1, 2, and 3 extend for three years, until June 30, 2021,\nprovisions of the Education Law relating to the implementation of IDEA.\n\nSection 4 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends provisions of Education Law that conform state statute\nto the federal Individuals with Disabilities Act of 2004. Federal fund-\ning for students with disabilities is contingent upon compliance with\nthe extension of IDEA. The current provisions of law will sunset on June\n30, 2018. Without an extender, New York's allocation of funds under IDEA\ncould be in jeopardy. This bill extends provisions of the Education Law\nfor three years until June 30, 2021 to ensure New York State continues\nto remain compliant and receive federal funding.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill, extends Chapter 35 of 2015.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone. Failure to continue the necessary provisions of law could place\nNew York's allocation of funds under IDEA in jeopardy.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall become effective on and after June 30, 2018.\n",
